{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | head -330'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl\n     2\t  \"The local Yin shell for DaoStream: explicit state, synchronous steps.\n     3\t\n     4\t   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock, or namespace\n     5\t   global.  It holds the one shell value a driver threads: the evaluator beside\n     6\t   its separately-owned program media — `program-in`, which the macro\n     7\t   expander observes, and `program-out`, which the evaluator's own observer\n     8\t   watches (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md` §10.1) — the language, the value\n     9\t   history, the output medium with its cursor, and a per-medium ledger\n    10\t   recording the last outcome that medium answered.  Every function takes a\n    11\t   state and returns the next one.\"\n    12\t  (:require #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    13\t               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n    14\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    15\t            [dao.pretty :as pretty]\n    16\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    17\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    18\t            [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    19\t            [yang.php :as yang.php]\n    20\t            [yang.python :as yang.python]\n    21\t            [yin.repl.link :as link]\n    22\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    23\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    24\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n    25\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as debruijn-linearize]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as register-compile]\n    28\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n    29\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n    30\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n    31\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    32\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n    33\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n    34\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    35\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    36\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(def output-capacity\n    40\t  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned output medium, in elements.\"\n    41\t  4096)\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def ingress-capacity\n    45\t  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned program medium, in elements.  The\n    46\t   shell is the only appender and its one step owner serializes evaluation, so\n    47\t   eviction can only follow a producer the composition does not make; a gap is\n    48\t   therefore fatal to the current evaluation rather than a normal operating\n    49\t   condition.\"\n    50\t  4096)\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(def drain-budget\n    54\t  \"Maximum elements one output drain reads.  It equals the output capacity,\n    55\t   so one drain reaches every element the medium still holds, the round's\n    56\t   result included.\"\n    57\t  output-capacity)\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(def gap-budget\n    61\t  \"Maximum `gap` answers one output drain accepts.  A gap is not an element,\n    62\t   so it is counted apart from `drain-budget`: a gap never costs the drain\n    63\t   an element, and the drain stays total against a transport that could\n    64\t   answer `gap` repeatedly.\"\n    65\t  4096)\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(def link-round-budget\n    69\t  \"How many serve-and-run rounds one evaluation drives while its VM waits\n    70\t   on a link (yin.vm.linker.md sections 6.3 and 7.2).  A round serves the\n    71\t   interpreter once and runs the VM once; a local content source answers\n    72\t   within a few, so the budget is reached only by a link that stays\n    73\t   `:pending`, which the shell then reports as its own non-blocking state\n    74\t   instead of wedging on.\"\n    75\t  40)\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def vm-constructors\n    79\t  \"The evaluators on `yin.vm`: the ast-walker, the linear semantic VM\n    80\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md`), and the nameless de Bruijn stack\n    81\t   and register kernels, each starting with an empty image.\"\n    82\t  {:ast-walker ast-walker/create-vm\n    83\t   :semantic semantic/create-vm\n    84\t   :stack #(stack/create-vm [] %)\n    85\t   :register #(register/create-vm nil %)})\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(def vm-labels\n    89\t  {:ast-walker \"ASTWalkerVM\"\n    90\t   :semantic \"SemanticVM\"\n    91\t   :stack \"DebruijnStackVM\"\n    92\t   :register \"DebruijnRegisterVM\"})\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(defn- packet->named-datoms\n    96\t  \"The named `:yin/*` datoms of one expanded tree packet, the input the de\n    97\t   Bruijn resolver reads.\"\n    98\t  [packet]\n    99\t  (vm/ast->datoms\n   100\t    (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (macro/packet->row-set packet))))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn- append-stack-image\n   104\t  \"Attach `image` after the stack image `vm` already holds and start at\n   105\t   its first instruction.  A closure a previous input stored (a `def`)\n   106\t   names a body pc in the earlier image, so that image is kept, not\n   107\t   replaced.  `stack/attach-image` admits the incoming image alone under\n   108\t   the current stamp (the expander and the lowerer are its fresh\n   109\t   producers), relocates and appends it, records its offset-table row,\n   110\t   and keeps `:hash` the canonical H of the whole `:segment`\n   111\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3).  Attaching touches no register, so\n   112\t   starting the input is this function's: `:pc` at the image's row, the\n   113\t   registers a fresh run starts with.  An input whose image is already\n   114\t   held reruns at that row.\"\n   115\t  [vm image]\n   116\t  (let [attached (stack/attach-image vm image vm/stack-contract)]\n   117\t    (assoc attached\n   118\t           :pc (stack/absolute-pc attached [(dcode/image-hash image) 0])\n   119\t           :frames []\n   120\t           :stack []\n   121\t           :continuation []\n   122\t           :halted? false\n   123\t           :blocked? false\n   124\t           :value nil)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- append-register-image\n   128\t  \"The register image counterpart of `append-stack-image`.  The image it\n   129\t   runs in is the concatenation, whose later main bodies end in `:halt` as\n   130\t   the first does, and `:hash` is the canonical R of that concatenation.\n   131\t   Starting the input sizes the register file for the main body at the\n   132\t   image's row.\"\n   133\t  [vm image]\n   134\t  (let [attached (register/attach-image vm image vm/register-contract)\n   135\t        pc (register/absolute-pc attached [(rcode/register-hash image) 0])\n   136\t        body (some #(when (= pc (:start %)) %)\n   137\t                   (:bodies (:segment attached)))]\n   138\t    (assoc attached\n   139\t           :pc pc\n   140\t           :frames []\n   141\t           :registers (vec (repeat (or (:registers body) 0) nil))\n   142\t           :continuation []\n   143\t           :halted? false\n   144\t           :blocked? false\n   145\t           :value nil)))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(def program-loaders\n   149\t  \"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\n   150\t   evaluator.  Every value there is one expanded canonical tree packet\n   151\t   `[root rows]` (yin.vm.macro.md §2.4); each loader takes its row set — the\n   152\t   ast-walker through `vm-load-rows`, the semantic VM through\n   153\t   `linearize/rows-loader` over `semantic/load-vector`, and the de Bruijn\n   154\t   kernels through their lowerings to a stack image (H) or a register\n   155\t   image (R).  No evaluator learns that an expander ran.\"\n   156\t  {:ast-walker (fn [vm packet]\n   157\t                 (ast-walker/vm-load-rows vm\n   158\t                                          (macro/packet->row-set packet)\n   159\t                                          vm/ast-contract))\n   160\t   ;; every loader here is the trusted fresh-producer path: the only\n   161\t   ;; producer of `program-out` is the expander, so each supplies the\n   162\t   ;; current stamp itself\n   163\t   :semantic (let [load-rows (linearize/rows-loader semantic/load-vector)]\n   164\t               (fn [vm packet]\n   165\t                 (load-rows vm\n   166\t                            (macro/packet->row-set packet)\n   167\t                            vm/ast-contract)))\n   168\t   :stack (fn [vm packet]\n   169\t            (append-stack-image\n   170\t              vm\n   171\t              (:image (debruijn-linearize/adapt\n   172\t                        (packet->named-datoms packet)))))\n   173\t   :register (fn [vm packet]\n   174\t               (append-register-image\n   175\t                 vm\n   176\t                 (:image (register-compile/adapt\n   177\t                           (packet->named-datoms packet)))))})\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t(def lang-labels {:clojure \"Clojure\" :python \"Python\" :php \"PHP\"})\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(def command-heads\n   184\t  \"Commands this shell answers.  `connect` and `disconnect` belong to the\n   185\t   driver, which owns the RPC client; `telemetry` is answered only to say that\n   186\t   this REPL slice does not have it.\"\n   187\t  #{'vm 'lang 'compile 'reset 'help 'repl-state 'quit 'telemetry 'abandon})\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t(def help-text\n   191\t  (str \"Commands:\\n\"\n   192\t       \"  (vm :ast-walker | :semantic | :stack | :register)\\n\"\n   193\t       \"  (lang :clojure | :python | :php)\\n\"\n   194\t       \"  (compile expr)\\n\"\n   195\t       \"  (reset)\\n\"\n   196\t       \"  (connect \\\"daostream:ws://host:port\\\")\\n\"\n   197\t       \"  (disconnect)\\n\"\n   198\t       \"  (abandon)  - give up a (require ...) that is still pending\\n\"\n   199\t       \"  (repl-state)\\n\"\n   200\t       \"  (help)\\n\"\n   201\t       \"  (quit)\\n\"\n   202\t       \"  *1, *2, *3  - last, second-to-last, and third-to-last evaluated\"\n   203\t       \" values\"))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(def telemetry-text\n   207\t  (str \"(telemetry) is not wired into this shell: the telemetry emit path is \"\n   208\t       \"built (yin.vm.telemetry, opt-in via the :telemetry {:stream ...} \"\n   209\t       \"construction option — yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md), but \"\n   210\t       \"composing a sink into this shell is not, so the command reports \"\n   211\t       \"rather than evaluates\"))\n   212\t\n   213\t\n   214\t(def ingress-loss-text\n   215\t  (str \"One or more program batches were never observed from the program \"\n   216\t       \"medium; (reset) is required before more evaluation\"))\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\t(def result-loss-text\n   220\t  \"the evaluation halted but its result never reached the output medium\")\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t;; =============================================================================\n   224\t;; Rendering\n   225\t;; =============================================================================\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn- quote-symbols\n   228\t  [x]\n   229\t  (cond (symbol? x) (list 'quote x)\n   230\t        (vector? x) (mapv quote-symbols x)\n   231\t        (map? x)\n   232\t        (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(quote-symbols k) (quote-symbols v)]) x))\n   233\t        (or (list? x) (seq? x))\n   234\t        (if (= 'quote (first x)) x (map quote-symbols x))\n   235\t        :else x))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn format-value\n   239\t  [value]\n   240\t  (str/trimr (pretty/pp-str (quote-symbols value))))\n   241\t\n   242\t\n   243\t(defn format-error\n   244\t  [error]\n   245\t  (str \"Error: \"\n   246\t       #?(:cljd (or (ex-message error) (str error))\n   247\t          :cljs (or (ex-message error) (.-message error) (str error))\n   248\t          :clj (or (ex-message error) (str error)))))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- print-arg\n   252\t  [value]\n   253\t  (if (string? value) value (format-value value)))\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\t(defn- print-text\n   257\t  [args]\n   258\t  (str/join \" \" (map print-arg args)))\n   259\t\n   260\t\n   261\t(defn- prn-text\n   262\t  [args]\n   263\t  (str (str/join \" \" (map format-value args)) \"\\n\"))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t;; =============================================================================\n   267\t;; The output medium\n   268\t;; =============================================================================\n   269\t\n   270\t(defn- emit-output!\n   271\t  [output-stream op text]\n   272\t  ;; A primitive holds no state, so it cannot record an append outcome.  The\n   273\t  ;; medium is an evict-oldest ring buffer, which never answers `full`; a closed\n   274\t  ;; medium drops the chunk and the drain reports the closure.\n   275\t  (when output-stream\n   276\t    (stream/append! output-stream {:type :repl/output :op op :text text}))\n   277\t  nil)\n   278\t\n   279\t\n   280\t(defn- emit-result!\n   281\t  \"Answer a halted evaluation's value on the output medium, after the\n   282\t   output it printed, so the shell reads results from the stream exactly as\n   283\t   it reads prints.  The token carries `round`, so the shell accepts only\n   284\t   this round's result.  Returns the append outcome, or `:untried` when\n   285\t   there is no medium.\"\n   286\t  [output-stream round value]\n   287\t  (if output-stream\n   288\t    (:dao.stream/outcome\n   289\t      (stream/append! output-stream\n   290\t                      {:type :repl/result :round round :value value}))\n   291\t    :untried))\n   292\t\n   293\t\n   294\t(defn- make-repl-primitives\n   295\t  [output-stream]\n   296\t  (merge vm/primitives\n   297\t         {'print (fn [& args]\n   298\t                   (emit-output! output-stream :print (print-text args)))\n   299\t          'println (fn [& args]\n   300\t                     (emit-output! output-stream :println\n   301\t                                   (str (print-text args) \"\\n\")))\n   302\t          'prn (fn [& args] (emit-output! output-stream :prn (prn-text args)))\n   303\t          'ast->datoms vm/ast->datoms\n   304\t          'datoms->ast vm/datoms->ast}))\n   305\t\n   306\t\n   307\t(defn- chunk-text\n   308\t  [value]\n   309\t  (if (map? value) (str (:text value)) (str value)))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- result-chunk?\n   313\t  [value]\n   314\t  (and (map? value) (= :repl/result (:type value))))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t(defn- ledger\n   318\t  [state medium outcome]\n   319\t  (assoc-in state [:ledger medium] outcome))\n   320\t\n   321\t\n   322\t(defn drain-output\n   323\t  \"Drain the output medium into `[state text results]`, total over every\n   324\t   `next` outcome.  `results` holds, in order, every `:repl/result` token\n   325\t   read, unchanged; every other element is printed text.\n   326\t\n   327\t   `ok` advances to the exact successor the handle returned and spends one\n   328\t   of `drain-budget` element reads.  `gap` prints a loss notice, resumes at\n   329\t   the recovery cursor, and spends one of `gap-budget` instead, so a gap\n   330\t   never starves the drain of an element it must still reach.  `end`,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
