{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '450,810p;930,1035p;1230,1275p'\"","aggregated_output":"   450\t                        (module/default-registry))\n   451\t             :make-stream make-ring-stream\n   452\t             ;; the task's capability secret (yin.vm.linker.md 7.3, r10):\n   453\t             ;; the REPL is the composition, so it mints one from its own\n   454\t             ;; random source, and a fresh one for every install child the\n   455\t             ;; task starts\n   456\t             :capability-secret (str (random-uuid))\n   457\t             :secret-source (fn [_origin] (str (random-uuid)))}\n   458\t      link-pair (assoc :link-request (:requests link-pair)\n   459\t                       :link-response (:responses link-pair))))))\n   460\t\n   461\t\n   462\t(defn- make-runner\n   463\t  \"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\n   464\t   VM through its protocol entry point, as a plain function so it can be\n   465\t   handed to observer coordination on every host, and answer a halted\n   466\t   run's value on `output-stream` under `round`.  The shell reads the value\n   467\t   from that stream, never from the VM record; the append outcome rides\n   468\t   back on the VM as `::result-append`, so a refused append is reported\n   469\t   rather than silently lost.\"\n   470\t  [output-stream round]\n   471\t  (fn [vm]\n   472\t    (let [vm' (vm/run vm)]\n   473\t      (if (vm/halted? vm')\n   474\t        (assoc vm'\n   475\t               ::result-append\n   476\t               (emit-result! output-stream round (vm/value vm')))\n   477\t        vm'))))\n   478\t\n   479\t\n   480\t(defn- make-attachment\n   481\t  \"Create one composition-owned medium of `capacity` elements, the unary\n   482\t   attachment entry bound to it for this medium's lifetime, and an observer\n   483\t   attached through that entry.\n   484\t\n   485\t   The resolver maps the descriptor's identity to the owner handle this\n   486\t   composition created, which is host composition around the ring buffer's own\n   487\t   attach mechanism: the observer itself sees only a descriptor and a unary\n   488\t   capability, so no transport detail crosses into it.\"\n   489\t  [capacity]\n   490\t  (let [writer (:dao.stream/handle\n   491\t                 (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   492\t                                ring/capacity-key capacity}))\n   493\t        described (stream/descriptor writer)\n   494\t        descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor described)\n   495\t        identity (:dao.stream/identity described)\n   496\t        attach! (ring/make-attacher {(:dao.stream/identity descriptor) writer})]\n   497\t    {:stream writer\n   498\t     :identity identity\n   499\t     :observer (observer/attach attach! descriptor)}))\n   500\t\n   501\t\n   502\t(defn- standard-store\n   503\t  \"The expander store seeded with the standard forms, folded through the\n   504\t   same row-native batch contract as any input (yin.vm.macro.md §5.4).\"\n   505\t  []\n   506\t  (macro/seed-store (macro/make-ctx {:token :yin.repl/standard-forms\n   507\t                                     :source-medium :yin.repl/standard-forms})\n   508\t                    [macro/stdlib-forms]))\n   509\t\n   510\t\n   511\t(defn- make-expander\n   512\t  \"The expander consumer for one session: a fresh incarnation token, the\n   513\t   `program-in` identity as its source medium, the standard store, and the\n   514\t   `program-out` writer.  No log writer: `(compile ...)` renders events.\"\n   515\t  [program-identity program-out]\n   516\t  (macro/make-expander\n   517\t    (macro/make-ctx {:token (str (random-uuid))\n   518\t                     :source-medium program-identity\n   519\t                     :store (standard-store)})\n   520\t    program-out))\n   521\t\n   522\t\n   523\t(defn- make-session\n   524\t  \"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\n   525\t   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\n   526\t   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\n   527\t   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\n   528\t   lifetime.\n   529\t\n   530\t   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\n   531\t   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\n   532\t   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n   533\t   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\n   534\t   which loads each packet and runs it.\n   535\t\n   536\t   The link pair is the session's (`yin.repl.link/make-pair`): the VM's\n   537\t   half lives in its private `:resources`, the interpreter's half beside\n   538\t   it under `:link-pair`.  The content pair and the name environment the\n   539\t   interpreter serves from are the shell's (`:link-source`), and outlive\n   540\t   a session rebuild.\"\n   541\t  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n   542\t  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n   543\t        vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives pair)\n   544\t        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\n   545\t        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n   546\t    {:vm vm\n   547\t     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\n   548\t     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\n   549\t     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n   550\t     :observer (:observer program-in)\n   551\t     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n   552\t     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n   553\t     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n   554\t     :link-pair pair}))\n   555\t\n   556\t\n   557\t(defn create-state\n   558\t  \"Create the shell value.  `:primitives` is a host-supplied map merged over\n   559\t   the REPL primitives; it is kept as `:extra-primitives` so every session\n   560\t   rebuild — `(reset)`, `(vm …)` — installs it again.\n   561\t\n   562\t   `content-store` (a `dao.jing` byte-store handle), `content-client` (a\n   563\t   `dao.stream.rpc` client state on a connection whose far end serves\n   564\t   content) and `name-env` (module name -> manifest address) compose the\n   565\t   content pair and the name environment the linker interpreter serves\n   566\t   `(require ...)` from (yin.repl.link/composition); with neither content\n   567\t   source, a require stays `:pending` and says so.\"\n   568\t  ([] (create-state {}))\n   569\t  ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n   570\t            content-store content-client name-env]\n   571\t     :or {lang :clojure vm-type :semantic}}]\n   572\t   (let [output-stream (or output-stream (make-output-medium!))\n   573\t         output-cursor (or output-cursor (mint-cursor output-stream))\n   574\t         link-source (link/composition\n   575\t                       {:name-env name-env\n   576\t                        :content-store content-store\n   577\t                        :content-client content-client})]\n   578\t     (merge\n   579\t       (make-session vm-type output-stream primitives)\n   580\t       {:lang lang\n   581\t        :vm-type vm-type\n   582\t        :extra-primitives primitives\n   583\t        :output-stream output-stream\n   584\t        :output-cursor output-cursor\n   585\t        :ledger {:output :untried}\n   586\t        :shell-token (str (random-uuid))\n   587\t        :round 0\n   588\t        :ingress-loss? false\n   589\t        :last-value nil\n   590\t        :last-value-2 nil\n   591\t        :last-value-3 nil\n   592\t        :pending-input nil\n   593\t        :link-source link-source\n   594\t        :pending-run nil\n   595\t        :running? true}))))\n   596\t\n   597\t\n   598\t;; =============================================================================\n   599\t;; Reading and classifying input\n   600\t;; =============================================================================\n   601\t\n   602\t(defn- read-forms\n   603\t  [input]\n   604\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n   605\t     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n   606\t     :clj (clojure.core/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))))\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- command-form?\n   610\t  [form]\n   611\t  (and (seq? form)\n   612\t       (symbol? (first form))\n   613\t       (contains? command-heads (first form))))\n   614\t\n   615\t\n   616\t(defn- datom?\n   617\t  [value]\n   618\t  (and (vector? value) (= 5 (count value))))\n   619\t\n   620\t\n   621\t(defn- datom-stream?\n   622\t  [value]\n   623\t  (and (vector? value) (seq value) (every? datom? value)))\n   624\t\n   625\t\n   626\t(defn- ast-map?\n   627\t  [value]\n   628\t  (and (map? value) (keyword? (:type value))))\n   629\t\n   630\t\n   631\t(defn- bracket-balance\n   632\t  \"Open minus close brackets, ignoring string literals and `;` comments.\n   633\t   Positive means the input is incomplete.\"\n   634\t  [s]\n   635\t  (loop [chars (seq s)\n   636\t         depth 0\n   637\t         in-str? false]\n   638\t    (if (empty? chars)\n   639\t      depth\n   640\t      (let [ch (first chars)\n   641\t            tail (rest chars)]\n   642\t        (cond in-str? (cond (= ch \\\\) (recur (rest tail) depth true)\n   643\t                            (= ch \\\") (recur tail depth false)\n   644\t                            :else (recur tail depth true))\n   645\t              (= ch \\\") (recur tail depth true)\n   646\t              (= ch \\;) (recur (drop-while #(not= % \\newline) tail) depth false)\n   647\t              (#{\\( \\[ \\{} ch) (recur tail (inc depth) false)\n   648\t              (#{\\) \\] \\}} ch) (recur tail (dec depth) false)\n   649\t              :else (recur tail depth false))))))\n   650\t\n   651\t\n   652\t;; =============================================================================\n   653\t;; Evaluation\n   654\t;; =============================================================================\n   655\t\n   656\t(defn- inject-last-value\n   657\t  [state]\n   658\t  (update state :vm update :store assoc\n   659\t          '*1 (:last-value state)\n   660\t          '*2 (:last-value-2 state)\n   661\t          '*3 (:last-value-3 state)))\n   662\t\n   663\t\n   664\t(defn- record-last-value\n   665\t  [state state-after value]\n   666\t  (assoc state-after\n   667\t         :last-value value\n   668\t         :last-value-2 (:last-value state)\n   669\t         :last-value-3 (:last-value-2 state)))\n   670\t\n   671\t\n   672\t(defn- round-id\n   673\t  \"The identity of the state's current round: the shell's token, minted\n   674\t   once per shell value, with its round count.  A medium the caller\n   675\t   supplies may already hold results from another shell or an earlier\n   676\t   round; none of them carries this identity.\"\n   677\t  [state]\n   678\t  [(:shell-token state) (:round state)])\n   679\t\n   680\t\n   681\t(defn- finalize-eval\n   682\t  \"Drain the round's output and its result from the output medium.  Only a\n   683\t   result stamped with this round's identity is this round's value; the\n   684\t   evaluator answers once per halted program, after its prints.  A missing\n   685\t   or foreign-round result is loss, reported with the append outcome the\n   686\t   runner recorded.\"\n   687\t  [state state' vm']\n   688\t  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n   689\t        [state'' output-text results]\n   690\t        (drain-output (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append)))\n   691\t        round (round-id state')\n   692\t        current (filterv #(= round (:round %)) results)]\n   693\t    (if (seq current)\n   694\t      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n   695\t        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n   696\t         (str output-text (format-value value))])\n   697\t      [state''\n   698\t       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text\n   699\t            (when (and append (not= :dao.stream/ok append))\n   700\t              (str \" (append: \" (name append) \")\")))])))\n   701\t\n   702\t\n   703\t(defn- drain-observer\n   704\t  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n   705\t   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n   706\t   stays nil.\"\n   707\t  [observer]\n   708\t  (when observer\n   709\t    (loop [observer observer]\n   710\t      (let [{:keys [status] observer' :observer}\n   711\t            (observer/observe-next observer)]\n   712\t        (if (#{:ok :gap} status) (recur observer') observer')))))\n   713\t\n   714\t\n   715\t(defn- consume-failed-round\n   716\t  \"Answer a round that threw with a recoverable shell state.\n   717\t\n   718\t   The failed input is consumed exactly once: each of the session's\n   719\t   observers resumes from the session the throw carried — the failing\n   720\t   stage's, matched by the medium it holds — or from where the round began\n   721\t   when it carried none, and reads past every batch still on its medium.\n   722\t   The shell is the only appender and appends one batch per round, so what\n   723\t   remains is the failed batch alone.  The VM is the one the round began\n   724\t   with, so a half-run continuation cannot be resumed — and its error\n   725\t   replayed — by the next input.  Output the round already emitted is\n   726\t   drained here, once.\"\n   727\t  [state error]\n   728\t  (let [carried (get-in (ex-data error) [:session :observer])\n   729\t        resume (fn [observer]\n   730\t                 (if (and observer\n   731\t                          carried\n   732\t                          (= (:stream carried) (:stream observer)))\n   733\t                   carried\n   734\t                   observer))\n   735\t        program (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n   736\t        rows (drain-observer (resume (:row-observer state)))\n   737\t        gaps-before (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n   738\t                       (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0))\n   739\t        gaps-after (+ (:ingress-gaps program 0) (:ingress-gaps rows 0))\n   740\t        [state' output-text]\n   741\t        (drain-output\n   742\t          (cond-> (assoc state :observer program :row-observer rows)\n   743\t            (> gaps-after gaps-before)\n   744\t            (assoc :ingress-loss? true)))]\n   745\t    [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))\n   746\t\n   747\t\n   748\t(defn- ingress-gaps\n   749\t  [state]\n   750\t  (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n   751\t     (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0)))\n   752\t\n   753\t\n   754\t(defn- run-expander-stage\n   755\t  \"Drive the expander over `program-in` and drain its summary.  It expands\n   756\t   each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n   757\t   failed expansion forwards nothing, yet its cursor advances (yin.vm.macro.md\n   758\t   decision 12).  Returns the state with the expander's progress and the\n   759\t   drained `{:errors :forwarded}` summary.\"\n   760\t  [state]\n   761\t  (let [{:keys [observer consumer]}\n   762\t        (macro/step {:observer (:observer state), :consumer (:expander state)})\n   763\t        [expander summary] (macro/drain-errors consumer)]\n   764\t    [(assoc state :observer observer :expander expander) summary]))\n   765\t\n   766\t\n   767\t(defn- run-evaluator-stage\n   768\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n   769\t   expanded tree packet into the VM, runs it, and answers its value on the\n   770\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n   771\t   the other.\"\n   772\t  [{:keys [load-program output-stream] :as state}]\n   773\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n   774\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n   775\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n   776\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n   777\t                                load-program\n   778\t                                (make-runner output-stream (round-id state)))]\n   779\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n   780\t\n   781\t\n   782\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n   783\t  [errors]\n   784\t  (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"Error: Macro expansion failed: \" (format-value %))\n   785\t                      errors)))\n   786\t\n   787\t\n   788\t(defn- link-waiting?\n   789\t  \"True while `vm` parks on a link wait: the two link states `require`\n   790\t   parks in, or the install it waits on (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2).\n   791\t   These are the reasons the shell's interpreter can move, so they are\n   792\t   the ones a round drives before reporting the VM wedged.\"\n   793\t  [vm]\n   794\t  (boolean (some #(contains? #{:link-request :link-response :install}\n   795\t                             (:reason %))\n   796\t                 (:wait-set vm))))\n   797\t\n   798\t\n   799\t(defn- carry-link-identity\n   800\t  \"The round's base VM with the link identity `used` has already minted\n   801\t   carried forward: link ids `[origin counter]` and install-child origin\n   802\t   tags are minted once and never reused on a pair (yin.vm.linker.md\n   803\t   section 7.2), and the shell's rollback to the round's base -- whose\n   804\t   counters never advanced -- must not let a later require or install\n   805\t   mint an identity the pair has already answered.\"\n   806\t  [base used]\n   807\t  (let [n (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) (or (:id-counter used) 0))\n   808\t        o (max (or (:origins base) 0) (or (:origins used) 0))]\n   809\t    (cond-> base\n   810\t      (pos? n) (assoc :id-counter n)\n   930\t        (let [[state' vm' pending] (drive-links evaluated vm)]\n   931\t          (cond\n   932\t            (vm/halted? vm')\n   933\t            (finalize-eval state\n   934\t                           (assoc state' :vm vm')\n   935\t                           (tokenize state'\n   936\t                                     (engine/restore-initial-env\n   937\t                                       (:env (:vm expanded)) vm')))\n   938\t\n   939\t            (link-waiting? vm')\n   940\t            (pending-eval state state' vm' pending)\n   941\t\n   942\t            :else (throw (wedged-program state))))\n   943\t\n   944\t        :else (throw (wedged-program state))))\n   945\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n   946\t      ;; a link raise rolls the shell back to the round's base; the\n   947\t      ;; identity the interrupted VM had minted rides on it, so nothing\n   948\t      ;; is minted twice on the surviving pair\n   949\t      (let [d (ex-data error)\n   950\t            base (if (or (::link-counter d) (::link-origins d))\n   951\t                   (carry-link-identity\n   952\t                     (:vm state)\n   953\t                     {:id-counter (::link-counter d)\n   954\t                      :origins (::link-origins d)})\n   955\t                   (:vm state))]\n   956\t        (consume-failed-round (assoc expanded :vm base) error)))))\n   957\t\n   958\t\n   959\t(defn- eval-program\n   960\t  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n   961\t   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n   962\t   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n   963\t   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n   964\t   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the evaluator only when a\n   965\t   program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n   966\t   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n   967\t   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n   968\t   is appended.\n   969\t\n   970\t   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n   971\t   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n   972\t   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n   973\t   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n   974\t   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n   975\t\n   976\t   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n   977\t   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n   978\t   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n   979\t  [state program]\n   980\t  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n   981\t    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n   982\t    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n   983\t          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n   984\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n   985\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n   986\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n   987\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n   988\t        (let [expanded (try\n   989\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n   990\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   991\t                                   :clj Exception\n   992\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n   993\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n   994\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n   995\t            failed\n   996\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded]\n   997\t              (cond\n   998\t                (> (ingress-gaps expanded) (ingress-gaps state'))\n   999\t                [(assoc expanded :ingress-loss? true)\n  1000\t                 (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1001\t\n  1002\t                (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state expanded)\n  1003\t\n  1004\t                :else [(assoc expanded :vm (:vm state))\n  1005\t                       (format-expansion-errors errors)]))))))))\n  1006\t\n  1007\t\n  1008\t(defn- compile-clojure-forms\n  1009\t  [forms]\n  1010\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n  1011\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n  1012\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n  1013\t\n  1014\t\n  1015\t(defn- compile-source\n  1016\t  [lang input]\n  1017\t  (case lang\n  1018\t    :clojure (compile-clojure-forms (read-forms input))\n  1019\t    :python (yang.python/compile input)\n  1020\t    :php (yang.php/compile input)\n  1021\t    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported Yin REPL language\" {:lang lang}))))\n  1022\t\n  1023\t\n  1024\t(defn- compile-command-ast\n  1025\t  [state arg]\n  1026\t  (case (:lang state)\n  1027\t    :clojure (if (string? arg)\n  1028\t               (compile-source :clojure arg)\n  1029\t               (yang.clojure/compile arg))\n  1030\t    (if (string? arg)\n  1031\t      (compile-source (:lang state) arg)\n  1032\t      (throw (ex-info \"This compile command expects a source string\"\n  1033\t                      {:lang (:lang state) :arg arg})))))\n  1034\t\n  1035\t\n  1230\t  (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n  1231\t        form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n  1232\t    (and form (command-form? form))))\n  1233\t\n  1234\t\n  1235\t(defn- eval-parsed\n  1236\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1237\t  (if (and (:pending-run state) (not (command-line? parsed)))\n  1238\t    ;; A require is still pending: re-check it first.  While it stays\n  1239\t    ;; pending the line is retained -- the parked VM owns the store a new\n  1240\t    ;; evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates, in typing order and\n  1241\t    ;; exactly once, when the link completes.\n  1242\t    (resume-pending state trimmed parsed)\n  1243\t    (eval-parsed* state trimmed parsed)))\n  1244\t\n  1245\t\n  1246\t(defn eval-input\n  1247\t  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n  1248\t\n  1249\t   Input whose brackets do not balance is retained as `:pending-input` and\n  1250\t   produces no text.  Nothing here is asynchronous: the driver, not this\n  1251\t   namespace, decides when the next step happens.\"\n  1252\t  [state line]\n  1253\t  (let [pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n  1254\t        combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n  1255\t                   (str/trim line)\n  1256\t                   (str pending \"\\n\" (str/trim line)))]\n  1257\t    (if (pos? (bracket-balance combined))\n  1258\t      [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n  1259\t      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n  1260\t            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n  1261\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1262\t                                  :clj Exception\n  1263\t                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n  1264\t                          {:error error}))]\n  1265\t        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n  1266\t\n  1267\t\n  1268\t(defn repl-state\n  1269\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n  1270\t\n  1271\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n  1272\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n  1273\t   operation.\n  1274\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n  1275\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
